    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "From eyewitness news, this is Newsmakers. Welcome to Newsmakers, I'm Tim White. Ted Nissi is on assignment. We are in a time of uncertainty. Fears over getting sick and fears of financial turmoil as more and more people are out of work. Thousands of Rhode Islanders have already applied for unemployment insurance. But for those of you who are independent contractors, that's not going to do you any good. Plus, test kits. The U.S. has been embarrassingly behind on screening citizens, putting more people at risk. When now, more than ever, knowledge is power. We are practicing social distancing here at WPRI-12, and that is why our guest Congressman David Sussolini is joining me on the telephone. Congressman, it's good to talk to you. Thank you for joining us, and I hope you're doing well.",
