    "turn_text": "Well, we have to be prepared to provide direct financial assistance to the tourism sector. You know, there's a lot of talk about airlines and You know, cruise ships, the reality is local restaurants, local arts and cultural organizations that are the lifeblood of the tourist economy in Rhode Island and in places all across the country need to be supported. These folks are going to have to essentially rebuild that part of our economy. And they're really important in terms of jobs. They're important in terms of the quality of life of our state. And what I'm learning is for sure, and I've spoken to the SBA administrator, it's not enough to provide just loans. For a lot of these small businesses, they need a direct grant. Sometimes it's, you know, 10 or 20,000 dollars just to stay open for the next two or three months to get through this difficult period. And I think we have to be prepared. And I think you will see in the House bill a direct grant program for small businesses, for business continuity to keep them open, to keep their operations open. and it's critical toward our economy and it's obviously critical to the nation's",
